H5900.definition:
from H5892 (עִיר); a citizen;
Iru, an Israelite
KJV: Iru.

H5901.definition:
from H5892 (עִיר); urbane;
Iri, an Israelite
KJV: Iri.

H5902.definition:
from H5892 (עִיר); city-wise;
Iram, an Idumaean
KJV: Iram.

H5903.definition:
or עֵרֹם; from H6191 (עָרַם);
nudity
KJV: naked(-ness).

H5904.definition:
from H5892 (עִיר) and H5175 (נָחָשׁ); city of a serpent;
Ir-Nachash, a place in Palestine
KJV: Irnahash.

H5905.definition:
from H5892 (עִיר) and H8121 (שֶׁמֶשׁ); city of the sun;
Ir-Shemesh, a place in Palestine
KJV: Irshemesh.

H5906.definition:
or עָשׁ; from H5789 (עוּשׁ);
the constellation of the Great Bear (perhaps from its migration through the heavens)
KJV: Arcturus.

H5907.definition:
probably for H5909 (עַכְבָּר);
Akbor, the name of an Idumaean and of two Israelites
KJV: Achbor.

H5908.definition:
probably from an unused root in the literal sense of entangling;
a spider (as weaving a network)
KJV: spider.

H5909.definition:
probably from the same as H5908 (עַכָּבִישׁ) in the secondary sense of attacking;
a mouse (as nibbling)
KJV: mouse.

H5910.definition:
apparently from an unused root meaning to hem in;
Akko (from its situation on a bay)
KJV: Accho.

H5911.definition:
from H5916 (עָכַר); troubled;
Akor, the name of a place in Palestine
KJV: Achor.

H5912.definition:
from an unused root meaning to trouble; troublesome;
Akan, an Israelite
KJV: Achan. Compare H5917 (עָכָר).

H5913.definition:
a primitive root; properly, to tie, specifically, with fetters; but used only as denominative from H5914 (עֶכֶס);
to put on anklets
KJV: make a tinkling ornament.

H5914.definition:
from H5913 (עָכַס);
a fetter; hence, an anklet
KJV: stocks, tinkling ornament.

H5915.definition:
feminine of H5914 (עֶכֶס); anklet;
Aksah, an Israelitess
KJV: Achsah.

H5916.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to roil water; figuratively, to disturb or affict
KJV: trouble, stir.

H5917.definition:
from H5916 (עָכַר); troublesome;
Akar, an Israelite
KJV: Achar. Compare H5912 (עָכָן).

H5918.definition:
from H5916 (עָכַר); muddler;
Okran, an Israelite
KJV: Ocran.

H5919.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to coil;
an asp (from lurking coiled up)
KJV: adder.

H5920.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
properly, the top; specifically, the highest (i.e. God); also (adverb) aloft, to Jehovah
KJV: above, high, most High.

H5921.definition:
properly, the same as H5920 (עַל) used as a preposition (in the singular or plural often with prefix, or as conjunction with a particle following);
above, over, upon, or against (yet always in this last relation with a downward aspect) in a great variety of applications
KJV: above, according to(-ly), after, (as) against, among, and, [idiom] as, at, because of, beside (the rest of), between, beyond the time, [idiom] both and, by (reason of), [idiom] had the charge of, concerning for, in (that), (forth, out) of, (from) (off), (up-) on, over, than, through(-out), to, touching, [idiom] with.

H5922.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5921 (עַל)
{above, over, upon, or against (yet always in this last relation with a downward aspect) in a great variety of applications}
KJV: about, against, concerning, for, (there-) fore, from, in, [idiom] more, of, (there-, up-) on, (in-) to, [phrase] why with.

H5923.definition:
or עוֹל; from H5953 (עָלַל);
a yoke (as imposed on the neck), literally or figuratively
KJV: yoke.

H5925.definition:
feminine of H5923 (עֹל); burden;
Ulla, an Israelite
KJV: Ulla.

H5926.definition:
from an unused root meaning to stutter;
stuttering
KJV: stammerer.

H5927.definition:
a primitive root;
to ascend, intransitively (be high) or actively (mount); used in a great variety of senses, primary and secondary, literal and figurative
KJV: arise (up), (cause to) ascend up, at once, break (the day) (up), bring (up), (cause to) burn, carry up, cast up, [phrase] shew, climb (up), (cause to, make to) come (up), cut off, dawn, depart, exalt, excel, fall, fetch up, get up, (make to) go (away, up); grow (over) increase, lay, leap, levy, lift (self) up, light, (make) up, [idiom] mention, mount up, offer, make to pay, [phrase] perfect, prefer, put (on), raise, recover, restore, (make to) rise (up), scale, set (up), shoot forth (up), (begin to) spring (up), stir up, take away (up), work.

H5928.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5930 (עֹלָה);
a holocaust
KJV: burnt offering.

H5929.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
a leaf (as coming up on a tree); collectively, foliage
KJV: branch, leaf.

H5930.definition:
or עוֹלָה; feminine active participle of H5927 (עָלָה);
a step or (collectively, stairs, as ascending); usually a holocaust (as going up in smoke)
KJV: ascent, burnt offering (sacrifice), go up to. See also H5766 (עֶוֶל).

H5931.definition:
(Aramaic) feminine from a root corresponding to H5927 (עָלָה);
a pretext (as arising artificially)
KJV: occasion.

H5932.definition:
for H5766 (עֶוֶל);
moral perverseness
KJV: iniquity.

H5933.definition:
or עַליָה; the same as H5932 (עַלְוָה);
Alvah or Aljah, an Idumaean
KJV: Aliah, Alvah.

H5934.definition:
passive participle of H5956 (עָלַם) in the denominative sense of H5958 (עֶלֶם);
(only in plural as abstract) adolescence; figuratively, vigor
KJV: youth.

H5935.definition:
or עַלְיָן; from H5927 (עָלָה); lofty;
Alvan or Aljan, an Idumaean
KJV: Alian, Alvan.

H5936.definition:
feminine passive participle of an unused root meaning to suck;
the leech
KJV: horse-leech.

H5937.definition:
a primitive root;
to jump for joy, i.e. exult
KJV: be joyful, rejoice, triumph.

H5938.definition:
from H5937 (עָלַז);
exultant
KJV: that rejoiceth.

H5939.definition:
feminine from an unused root meaning to cover;
dusk
KJV: dark, twilight.

H5940.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
a pestle (as lifted)
KJV: pestle.

H5941.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה); lofty;
Eli, an Israelite highpriest
KJV: Eli.

H5942.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
high; i.e. comparative
KJV: upper.

H5943.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5942 (עִלִּי);
supreme (i.e. God)
KJV: (most) high.

H5944.definition:
feminine from H5927 (עָלָה);
something lofty, i.e. a stair-way; also a second-story room (or even one on the roof); figuratively, the sky
KJV: ascent, (upper) chamber, going up, loft, parlour.

H5945.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
an elevation, i.e. (adj.) lofty (compar.); as title, the Supreme
KJV: (Most, on) high(-er, -est), upper(-most).

H5946.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5945 (עֶלְיוֹן);
the Supreme
KJV: Most high.

H5947.definition:
from H5937 (עָלַז);
exultant
KJV: joyous, (that) rejoice(-ing)

H5948.definition:
from H5953 (עָלַל) in the sense of completing;
probably a crucible (as working over the metal)
KJV: furnace.

H5949.definition:
or עֲלִלָה; from H5953 (עָלַל) in the sense of effecting;
an exploit (of God), or a performance (of man, often in a bad sense); by implication, an opportunity
KJV: act(-ion), deed, doing, invention, occasion, work.

H5952.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
a second-story room
KJV: chamber. Compare H5944 (עֲלִיָּה).

H5953.definition:
a primitive root;
to effect thoroughly; specifically, to glean (also figuratively); by implication (in a bad sense) to overdo, i.e. maltreat, be saucy to, pain, impose (also literal)
KJV: abuse, affect, [idiom] child, defile, do, glean, mock, practise, thoroughly, work (wonderfully).

H5955.definition:
feminine active participle of H5953 (עָלַל);
only in plural gleanings; by extension gleaning-time
KJV: (gleaning) (of the) grapes, grapegleanings.

H5956.definition:
a primitive root;
to veil from sight, i.e. conceal (literally or figuratively)
KJV: [idiom] any ways, blind, dissembler, hide (self), secret (thing).

H5957.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5769 (עוֹלָם);
remote time, i.e. the future or past indefinitely; often adverb, forever
KJV: for (n-)ever (lasting), old.

H5958.definition:
from H5956 (עָלַם); (compare H5959 (עַלְמָה))
properly, something kept out of sight, i.e. a lad
KJV: young man, stripling.

H5959.definition:
feminine of H5958 (עֶלֶם);
a lass (as veiled or private)
KJV: damsel, maid, virgin.

H5961.definition:
plural of H5959 (עַלְמָה);
properly, girls, i.e. the soprano or female voice, perhaps falsetto
KJV: Alamoth.

H5962.definition:
(Aramaic) patrial from a name corresponding to H5867 (עֵילָם) contracted;
an Elamite or inhabitant of Elam
KJV: Elamite.

H5963.definition:
from the same as H5960 (עַלְמוֹן) and the dual of H1960 (הֻיְּדָה) (compare H1015 (בֵּית דִּבְלָתַיִם)) with enclitic of direction; Almon towards Diblathajim;
Almon-Diblathajemah, a place in Moab
KJV: Almondilathaim.

H5964.definition:
from H5956 (עָלַם); a covering;
Alemeth, the name of a place in Palestine and of two Israelites
KJV: Alameth, Alemeth.

H5965.definition:
a primitive root;
to leap for joy, i.e. exult, wave joyously
KJV: [idiom] peacock, rejoice, solace self.

H5966.definition:
a primitive root;
to sip up
KJV: suck up.

H5967.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6763 (צֵלָע);
a rib
KJV: rib.

H5968.definition:
a primitive root;
to veil or cover; figuratively, to be languid
KJV: faint, overlaid, wrap self.

H5969.definition:
from H5968 (עָלַף);
an envelope, i.e. (figuratively) mourning
KJV: fainted.

H5970.definition:
a primitive root;
to jump for joy, i.e. exult
KJV: be joyful, rejoice, triumph.

H5971.definition:
from H6004 (עָמַם);
a people (as a congregated unit); specifically, a tribe (as those of Israel); hence (collectively) troops or attendants; figuratively, a flock
KJV: folk, men, nation, people.

H5972.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5971 (עַם)
{a people (as a congregated unit); specifically, a tribe (as those of Israel); hence (collectively) troops or attendants; figuratively, a flock}
KJV: people.

H5973.definition:
from H6004 (עָמַם);
adverb or preposition, with (i.e. in conjunction with), in varied applications; specifically, equally with; often with prepositional prefix (and then usually unrepresented in English)
KJV: accompanying, against, and, as ([idiom] long as), before, beside, by (reason of), for all, from (among, between), in, like, more than, of, (un-) to, with(-al).

H5974.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5973 (עִם)
{adverb or preposition, with (i.e. in conjunction with), in varied applications; specifically, equally with; often with prepositional prefix (and then usually unrepresented in English)}
KJV: by, from, like, to(-ward), with.

H5975.definition:
a primitive root;
to stand, in various relations (literal and figurative, intransitive and transitive)
KJV: abide (behind), appoint, arise, cease, confirm, continue, dwell, be employed, endure, establish, leave, make, ordain, be (over), place, (be) present (self), raise up, remain, repair, [phrase] serve, set (forth, over, -tle, up), (make to, make to be at a, with-) stand (by, fast, firm, still, up), (be at a) stay (up), tarry.

H5976.definition:
for H4571 (מָעַד);
to shake
KJV: be at a stand.

H5977.definition:
from H5975 (עָמַד);
a spot (as being fixed)
KJV: place, ([phrase] where) stood, upright.

H5978.definition:
prolonged for H5973 (עִם);
along with
KJV: against, by, from, [phrase] me, [phrase] mine, of, [phrase] that I take, unto, upon, with(-in.)

H5979.definition:
from H5975 (עָמַד);
a station, i.e. domicile
KJV: standing.

H5980.definition:
from H6004 (עָמַם);
conjunction, i.e. society; mostly adverb or preposition (with prepositional prefix), near, beside, along with
KJV: (over) against, at, beside, hard by, in points.

H5981.definition:
the same as H5980 (עֻמָּה); association;
Ummah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ummah.

H5982.definition:
or עַמֻּד; from H5975 (עָמַד);
a column (as standing); also a stand, i.e. platform
KJV: [idiom] apiece, pillar.

H5983.definition:
from H5971 (עַם); tribal, i.e. inbred;
Ammon, a son of Lot; also his posterity and their country
KJV: Ammon, Ammonites.

H5984.definition:
patronymically from H5983 (עַמּוֹן);
an Ammonite or (the adjective) Ammonitish
KJV: Ammonite(-s).

H5985.definition:
feminine of H5984 (עַמּוֹנִי);
an Ammonitess
KJV: Ammonite(-ss).

H5986.definition:
from H6006 (עָמַס); burdensome;
Amos, an Israelite prophet
KJV: Amos.

H5987.definition:
from H6009 (עָמַק); deep;
Amok, an Israelite
KJV: Amok.

H5988.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H410 (אֵל); people of God;
Ammiel, the name of three or four Israelites
KJV: Ammiel.

H5989.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H1935 (הוֹד); people of splendor;
Ammihud, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Ammihud.

H5990.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H2064 (זָבַד); people of endowment;
Ammizabad, an Israelite
KJV: Ammizabad.

H5991.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H2353 (חוּר); people of nobility;
Ammichur, a Syrian prince
KJV: Ammihud (from the margin).

H5992.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H5068 (נָדַב); people of liberality;
Amminadab, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Amminadab.

H5993.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H5081 (נָדִיב); my people (is) liberal;
Ammi-Nadib, probably an Israelite
KJV: Amminadib.

H5994.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6012 (עָמֵק);
profound, i.e. unsearchable
KJV: deep.

H5995.definition:
from H6014 (עָמַר);
a bunch of grain
KJV: handful, sheaf.

H5996.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H7706 (שַׁדַּי); people of (the) Almighty;
Ammishaddai, an Israelite
KJV: Ammishaddai.

H5997.definition:
from a primitive root meaning to associate;
companionship; hence (concretely) a comrade or kindred man
KJV: another, fellow, neighbour.

H5998.definition:
a primitive root;
to toil, i.e. work severely and with irksomeness
KJV: (take) labour (in).

H5999.definition:
from H5998 (עָמַל);
toil, i.e. wearing effort; hence, worry, wheth. of body or mind
KJV: grievance(-vousness), iniquity, labour, mischief, miserable(-sery), pain(-ful), perverseness, sorrow, toil, travail, trouble, wearisome, wickedness.
